  "brand": "Proprietary Systems",
  "suiteName": "Proprietary Systems",
  "positioning": "One intelligent operating system for the entire business.",
  "principles": [
    "A customer business is the tenant; products are capabilities inside its operating environment.",
    "The suite is industry-agnostic and configured through shared objects, workflows, permissions, and templates.",
    "Every employee product enters through the suite even when security, compliance, or scale justify a separate runtime and data plane.",
    "A hostname is a durable user or technical boundary, not a reason to duplicate a repository.",
    "Canonical employee product pages and application routes use the unified marketing and application hosts; bounded APIs remain separate only when operations, compliance, or data architecture require it.",
    "Client brands and delivery sites are tenants or external surfaces, never Proprietary Systems products."
  ],
